  "title": {
   "en": "Gokuraku ni Itaru Imimon"
  },
  "altTitles": [
   {
    "ja": "極楽に至る忌門"
   },
   {
    "en": "The Forbidden Gate to Paradise"
   }
  ],
  "description": {
   "en": "A small village deep in the mountains of Shikoku. There, a strange Buddha statue is enshrined. Hayato comes from Tokyo to the village to accompany his friend Takumi on a trip back home, but he feels something is off about the villagers' strange cold demeanor... Takumi's grandmother warmly welcomes him, and in the middle of a peaceful dinner, the moment she says \"you have brought the Buddha closer,\" Takumi's face changes color and disappears that night. From there, Hayato becomes embroiled in a series of strange events.",
   "ja": "四国の山奥にある小さな村。そこには奇妙な仏像があり、大切に祀られていた。\n友人・匠の帰省に付き添い、東京から村へ訪れた隼人は、村人たちの異様に冷たい空気に違和感を抱く…。\n匠の祖母に優しく迎えられ、和やかな夕食の最中、「仏を近づけた」という祖母の言葉を聞いた瞬間、匠が顔色を変え、家を飛び出し――その夜、失踪。\n隼人はそこから立て続けに起きる奇妙なことに巻き込まれていく。\n恐ろしい土地の因縁と、怪異。\n匠の祖母の言った「仏」とは何なのか、その正体が顔を出す第一章「頷き仏」の開幕"
  },
